From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:29:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8011-pro2: Speakers, charging, light
 sensors, 120 Hz

The iPad Pro 2 hardware that tompta1 brought up on his J120 (#205,
09038adf) and that the first integration left out, in the shared iPad
Pro 2 device tree:

- the four MAX98723 speaker amplifiers on I2C1/I2C2 and the MCA2 TDM
  link (SmartIO endpoints 0x2c/0x2d), one "Jxxx Speakers" card per board;
- the D2355 Lightning charger with the cbtl1610 Tristar, its PMU events
  on AP GPIO 204, the August ADC, the pack window and the 1.5 A board
  maximum guarded by the Bellatrix VBUS reading on I2C1;
- both CT709 ambient light sensors on I2C3, als0 for the calibration;
- the H9G display registers, named by the boot framebuffer for the
  120 Hz cadence;
- the Smart Cover through his polled two-sensor driver instead of the
  single-line gpio-keys-polled description, which was never run on a
  J120; the hall events stay wake events;
- his bounded HDQ transport for the battery gauge.

The J120 alone also names its PCIe controller, for his NVMe write
limits. Device tree nodes from his t8011 patches 0003-0020, moved to
where main describes the boards.

Assisted-by: LLM
